Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Index conventions and contraction path", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb5767-1f00-4973-a411-49eacd07850d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This tech note pins down the index conventions the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "Wolfram"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c0a03138-f6f5-48b2-9650-24cdd7a1175c"],
 "TensorNetworks`` kernel uses and shows how the ",
 StyleBox["same", "TI"],
 " contraction reads in each one. The conventions look alike (everything is a \
list of small integers) but they count different things, and conflating them \
is the usual source of confusion. We work computation-first: every claim \
below is produced by a cell you can rerun, and we read the meaning off the \
output rather than asserting it."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"339b4dd0-83de-464f-8575-c0a0b80d881a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Five conventions appear. Four of them number ",
 StyleBox["legs",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", where a ",
 StyleBox["leg", "TI"],
 " is a single index of a tensor (one of its axes); one numbers ",
 StyleBox["operands",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", where an ",
 StyleBox["operand", "TI"],
 " is a whole tensor taking part in a contraction. The operands are not \
fixed: at the start they are the input tensors, and each contraction step \
replaces the two tensors it combines with their single result, so an operand \
can be an original input or an intermediate produced by an earlier step. \
Keeping the leg-versus-operand split in mind answers most questions on sight: \
when you see a list of integer pairs, ask \"pairs of ",
 StyleBox["what", "TI"],
 "\", legs or operands."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"45be605a-001a-4029-a66a-d36373bb1564"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "08341701-ad31-4841-955e-ce813d0948ea"], Cell["Convention", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"3721c115-2931-481f-8be6-e29559c59274"],
     Cell["An integer means", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"c88f2f90-7270-405f-98af-8965325c96e8"],
     Cell["A contraction is written as", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"0129341e-4021-4f86-bc7c-130326d7b6eb"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "3a05c056-9cec-428c-bf0e-40949950cb68"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
     "EinsteinSummation"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
      "9796787b-363b-4edb-801f-978855832dfa"],
     " label"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"2ad226ac-2bf3-4ded-bdee-8682f1301201"], 
    Cell["an abstract name", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "89062e22-04a9-4e9f-9c6c-cb1b22116b01"], Cell[
    "the same name on two tensors", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "de3c1f2e-8b42-45ce-acb8-50b9636e04f4"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "fef0a68c-659b-4953-b7a0-c2ce91918391"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
     "TensorNetwork"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
      "189955ed-ffb9-46cb-9d8b-3ad838bd1ae0"],
     " data label"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"42717e1d-a897-48f5-af1c-2b4708741989"], 
    Cell["a tensor-position, leg-label tag per leg", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"0eeb4f25-64ca-4373-948a-d27f40190b18"], Cell[
    "a bond group (the legs sharing a label)", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2333e9ca-f96f-43c1-8b66-2849c6cfd844"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "f799c708-215c-4b88-8268-bf5bc5e4d316"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
     "TensorContract"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
      "828fdcdb-76fd-4198-ae40-9f301a88d18f"],
     " global slot"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1c883d34-8aa8-4272-bb71-b3eddbb3552a"], 
    Cell[TextData[{
     "a slot in the flattened ",
     Cell[BoxData[
     "TensorProduct"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
      "a3677cfc-faab-4d14-93cc-a06c8b9db52a"]
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"a935ad6a-29c3-410e-93b4-4dbaf8c73be2"], 
    Cell["a pair of global slots", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "6f983e97-6e1a-4189-b654-bd972dc426cf"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "eb6beb12-be2b-4a56-8210-057ecc83c44c"], Cell[TextData[{
     Cell[BoxData[
     "ArrayDot"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
      "7a8040bd-3d26-4268-8848-79894d8abd6b"],
     " operand-local axis"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"e4a72278-8635-4718-8640-826ca4e601fe"], 
    Cell["an axis within one operand", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "e7a9dd62-ef9a-45bc-90be-4f2e731e8bca"], Cell[
    "a pair of operand-local axes", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "ccfd19ec-31c3-4069-9bbd-7bdf2207b4b9"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "7c440cb6-1a61-460d-9d2f-bb0ec7b17131"], Cell[
    "contraction-path position", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "c1052636-6973-4e1e-823d-dbab9496c01c"], Cell[
    "a position in the operand list", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "3f89b7ce-9752-408a-9415-348d452bf74a"], Cell[
    "a pair of operands to multiply", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "f456d995-3e18-47aa-a1a9-8d059e0ffec8"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"bb529094-7ef1-4698-ac4a-\
d52fea4b5d7f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three of these four leg conventions give a leg a fixed identity, no matter \
how the network is contracted; the fourth, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "ArrayDot"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d491fda9-06e3-4b96-b0e9-c0b766de9b1e"],
 " operand-local axes, is meaningful only during a contraction step. We build \
one small network, read its indices in those three fixed conventions, then \
see how a contraction path (operands) and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "ArrayDot"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9163e1c3-121e-47ef-8709-659184f6b28e"],
 " (operand-local axes) re-express the same sums, and close with the two \
cases a repeated index can take beyond a plain pairwise contraction: \
broadcasting and hyperedges. Each section re-creates the running network so \
it stands on its own."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"33e73b7f-5016-4161-bf9c-ba664aad7e50"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Load tensor network paclet:", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.98967587312405*^9, 3.9896758796101303`*^9}},
 CellID->292596168,ExpressionUUID->"da335d66-c4e7-400f-bbd5-92bb690bd857"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`TensorNetworks`\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9896758824062634`*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[6]:=",
 CellID->164351263,ExpressionUUID->"7618fdc4-c450-4920-ad2e-2e727e713602"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Setup: one small network", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4c28fa79-3c03-446e-928f-e14f927f6773"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We use three tensors in a chain, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "EinsteinSummation"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7f6427bd-78de-4b3c-a4ab-69aa1246ddc9"],
 " labels ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b7d89c1b-c186-4339-b075-59aaafb10c4d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["j", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8df4b7d2-eb78-4c1d-8a1a-9807a139fdc6"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8e43873a-1805-45b6-9014-5256b163c408"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["l", "TI"], "=", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "bc5d90e5-5427-461e-9472-306c7f271f6a"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", "5"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5f6555d1-cdb4-4a8a-9901-08b0625ef06e"],
 ": ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "t1"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "330ed271-075f-4314-b1df-904616c3ec31"],
 " carries ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{",", "\[ThinSpace]"}], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]}], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a85758e1-eca4-4553-9dc0-c63c0f485bcf"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "t2"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "21971ccc-49e4-4c6f-9bbc-de9fc5073adc"],
 " carries ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{",", "\[ThinSpace]"}], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{",", "\[ThinSpace]"}], 
    StyleBox["l", "TI"]}], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f4789bdd-a8e1-468b-b096-0970f8acf57d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "t3"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1c5090f2-e834-4092-90dd-bb422e63cb81"],
 " carries ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{",", "\[ThinSpace]"}], 
    StyleBox["l", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{",", "\[ThinSpace]"}], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "1fbf84e8-6e3b-4fce-bb6c-035e1953ca50"],
 ". So ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9b7d72b4-f5eb-4cd3-b0d1-5cf3ccb93774"],
 " is a bond between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "t1"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "fdd421b7-6a6c-4759-a302-dbae60ac5592"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "t2"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "927eaa82-1971-4e82-9d85-3e13b767c4cb"],
 ", while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "100a16f9-d485-4b00-90ab-abb3580b3e24"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["l", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8f1957bb-2f3c-4edf-8667-185bff064ac3"],
 " are ",
 StyleBox["two", "TI"],
 " bonds between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "t2"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "20736b7f-fc85-46ff-9175-b8bc1beb2cd5"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "t3"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "0f7113c2-abf1-4115-b27a-433a7fc8607e"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2cc30777-5b93-43a8-9418-33ff4ea1090d"],
 " (on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "t1"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "788043b1-31ef-40fb-adb2-10482f4a11df"],
 ") and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ce77a3ec-cecb-413d-87b3-aac889170053"],
 " (on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "t3"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7c826723-7cbd-429b-9ba1-66b0b2ddf77c"],
 ") are the free legs. We ask for the output in the natural order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{",", "\[ThinSpace]"}], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "733ee0f0-809f-4f59-86a0-5ac0c718baaa"],
 ". We use symbolic arrays (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ArraySymbol",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/ArraySymbol"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "aba11b48-07a4-4b81-b27b-f5a1df46a577"],
 ") so the structural outputs display by name rather than as numbers."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a36c2589-2665-41a1-a7ef-22ab8b6d7ad0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Define the tensors and the network:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6a88bdc0-6865-4534-9679-3d34d0693416"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"t1", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ArraySymbol", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<t1\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"t2", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ArraySymbol", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<t2\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"t3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ArraySymbol", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<t3\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "5", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"tn", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"TensorNetwork", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"t1", ",", " ", "t2", ",", " ", "t3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], " ", "->",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b529cdef-55cb-47a9-85f1-154b81e75cd3"],

